<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Craftsmanship</h1>
<p>Craftsmanship is how well a weapon, a shield or a piece of armour was 
made. It ranges from worthless to godly; average is ordinary work. The 
identify spells tell you an item's craftsmanship, in words such as poor, 
good, superior or godly (see <a cmd='#'>Help Identify</a>).
</p><p>Craftsmanship counts in every fight, much like an item's magic:
</p>
<ul><li>a well made <b>weapon</b> hits more easily and harder;</li>
<li>well made <b>armour</b> turns blows better;</li>
<li>a well made <b>shield</b> blocks better.</li></ul>
<p>It also decides how much wear an item can take before it breaks: fine 
work lasts several times longer than average work, and poor work wears out 
fast.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
